# Sable Reach and the desert
plate: doc
dh: Covenant Registry | DOMINION OF SABLE · SABLE REACH
df: Candidate | VOSS, Zara · twenty-one
df: Nominated by | her mother (TR)
df: Mother | Unbound · raised her alone
df: Father | unnamed (TR)
df: Desert name | not on file
stamp: COVENANT DAUGHTER
/end
rec:
Her grandmother | Her real name is one the desert knows and the Empire doesn't. She raised Zara with the Sable education: the land, the plants, and the patience of someone who reads an environment that kills you if you misread it (TR).
Her father | Unnamed, the way the desert is unnamed. It exists, it shaped everything, and it doesn't need documentation (TR).
Her Dominion | The Empire sees the desert and sees geography to manage. Sable women see a teacher (TR). The Empire renamed the cities and not the land, and the scoring process has no rubric for silence as calculation (DOM).
In the Trials | The Trial has had three cycles to learn what two Sable women are worth, and hasn't adjusted. Zara's been counting on that (TR).
prompt: What her grandmother taught her first | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · XI · ZARA · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 1 OF 2" m="TKC: TR · TL · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:sable} · {v1:lived5}"
# What she believes
rec:
Who taught her | Her grandmother and the desert (TR). The Finding, a girl left at a family site from sunset to sunrise, and what she brings back becomes her adult name in the community (DOM).
What she carries | Two names, as Sable women do, one the Empire knows and one that lives in the house where it can't reach (TR). Hers is Tazaleh (TL).
What she practices | The Desert Walk before a Binding. The dead given back to the desert, the name said once into a fire that nobody puts out (DOM).
empire: What the Temple teaches about a woman like her
The Empire doesn't know desert names exist (DOM). POSSIBLE: The Temple teaches that the name the Registry holds is the name God knows.
/end
prompt: What she brought back from the Finding, and how it became Tazaleh | fill

@page rh="THE COVENANT DAUGHTERS · XI · ZARA · FAITH AND SCRIPTURE · 2 OF 2" m="GEN 38.27–30; MATT 1.3; GEN 16.13; ISA 35.1; REV 2.17; DEUT 8.2"
# The text
rec:
Her name | *Zara* is the King James spelling of Zerah, Tamar's twin (Matt 1.3, Gen 38.30, Vol. I, {v1:cast}). At the birth his hand comes out first and the midwife ties a scarlet thread on it, "This came out first." His brother breaks out ahead of him (Gen 38.28–30).
Where it breaks | POSSIBLE: Zerah is marked first and born second, and the royal line runs through his brother. Zara is marked last and doesn't stay there.
Hagar · Genesis 16 | POSSIBLE: A woman alone in the desert who names God, "Thou God seest me" (16.13). **Where it breaks:** Hagar is found in the desert. Zara was raised to be at home in it.
tab:
| She'd quote | Never read to her |
| Isaiah 35.1, "the desert shall rejoice, and blossom as the rose" | Revelation 2.17, a white stone with "a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it" |
| Genesis 16.13, "Thou God seest me" | Genesis 38, which the Temple doesn't teach (Vol. I, {v1:tamar}) |
box: Volume One
Sable, {v1:sable}. Lived religion, {v1:lived5}. Tamar and the twins, {v1:tamar}. Hagar, {v1:hagar}. The names in the cast, {v1:cast}.
/end

